From: Dynamic Devices <info@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: leave symbol stripping to the packaging system

Yocto splits debugging symbols and strips runtime binaries during packaging.
Stripping at link time prevents that split and fails already-stripped QA.
Keep the Release garbage collection and as-needed linker options, but leave
the symbol table intact for the packaging task.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto packaging owns debug splitting and stripping]

---
 Data/CMake/LinkerGC.cmake | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Data/CMake/LinkerGC.cmake b/Data/CMake/LinkerGC.cmake
--- a/Data/CMake/LinkerGC.cmake
+++ b/Data/CMake/LinkerGC.cmake
@@ -2,7 +2,6 @@
 
 # This applies some common linker options that reduce code size and linking time in Release mode. Namely:
 # --gc-sections: Linktime garbage collection, discards unused sections from the final output
-# --strip-all  : Similar to running `strip`, discards the symbol table from the final output
 # --as-needed  : Only includes libraries that are actually needed in the final output.
 
 macro(LinkerGC target)
@@ -9,7 +8,6 @@ macro(LinkerGC target)
   if (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE MATCHES "RELEASE")
     target_link_options(${target} PRIVATE
       "LINKER:--gc-sections"
-      "LINKER:--strip-all"
       "LINKER:--as-needed")
   endif()
 endmacro()
